From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AtlasYang <atlas.yang3598@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:49:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan_encode: release the packet buffer of pictures freed
 before output

vulkan_encode_issue() takes a host-visible bitstream buffer from the
pool into vp->pkt_buf, and only vulkan_encode_output() hands it on, to
the packet or to ctx->prev_buf_ref. A picture that is issued but never
output, because the encoder is closed before it is drained or because
issue fails after taking the buffer, is freed through
vulkan_encode_free_pic() with its reference still held. The pool is
uninitialised, but it lives on while a buffer is out, so the VkBuffer,
its memory and its mapping (3 * width * height + 64 KiB, about 6 MiB at
1080p) stay for the life of the process. A long-running process that
cancels encodes accumulates one per close.

Unref vp->pkt_buf when a picture is freed, and ctx->prev_buf_ref on
uninit, which holds the buffer of a non-independent frame until the
next picture is output. The execution context holds its own reference
while the GPU writes the buffer, and ff_vulkan_encode_uninit() waits on
the execution pool before freeing the queued pictures.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 libavcodec/vulkan_encode.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavcodec/vulkan_encode.c b/libavcodec/vulkan_encode.c
index 1e69c73242..880a4b7a09 100644
--- a/libavcodec/vulkan_encode.c
+++ b/libavcodec/vulkan_encode.c
@@ -46,6 +46,9 @@ static void vulkan_encode_free_pic(FFVulkanEncodeContext *ctx,
     vp->in.view = VK_NULL_HANDLE;
     vp->dpb.view = VK_NULL_HANDLE;
 
+    /* Only set if the picture was issued but never output */
+    av_buffer_unref(&vp->pkt_buf);
+
     ctx->slots[vp->dpb_slot.slotIndex] = NULL;
 }
 
@@ -68,6 +71,9 @@ av_cold void ff_vulkan_encode_uninit(FFVulkanEncodeContext *ctx)
     for (FFHWBaseEncodePicture *pic = ctx->base.pic_start; pic; pic = pic->next)
         vulkan_encode_free_pic(ctx, pic);
 
+    /* Held across pictures for a non-independent frame */
+    av_buffer_unref(&ctx->prev_buf_ref);
+
     av_buffer_pool_uninit(&ctx->buf_pool);
 
     ff_hw_base_encode_close(&ctx->base);
-- 
